@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

#
# prima-materia — the third protocol opened against a generalization, and the
# first one run against the claim the whole holding is built around
#
# The claim examined is the one with the most witnesses in the file of
# generalizations, nine, and it is also the one this project would least like to
# be wrong about: that a transmission whose success cannot be checked apart from
# itself supplies, in advance, a place to put the run that produced nothing.
#
# It named its own falsifying case and it named three addresses at which to look
# for it. All three were visited. None of them refutes it, and the reason is the
# same at each: the corpus that names the sign also prints the excuse, in the
# same chapter or in the chapter next to it.
#
# The deviation came from the other direction, from the counter-search that
# prima-materia#726 was opened to make obligatory. It was run here for the first
# time as a separate griff, and it returned a case at once.
#

pmp:WhereTheEmptyRunIsPutExamination a pm:Testing ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the empty run is always assigned to a party"@en, "Ob der leere Durchgang immer einer Partei zugewiesen wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "A protocol on the claim that where a transmission prescribes an operation whose success cannot be established apart from the operation itself, the same transmission supplies a condition under which a run that produced nothing counts as no failure, and locates that condition in the operator, in the person operated on, in the material or in a third party. Two questions were put to the holding and not one: whether a transmission of the kind described supplies no such condition at all, which is the falsifying case the claim names; and whether one supplies it and puts it somewhere the claim's enumeration does not allow."@en ;
    pm:tests pmc:NoFailedRunCountsAgainstTheOperation ;
    pm:falsifiedBy "A transmission of the kind described whose earliest witness names an outcome that would count against the operation and supplies no condition assigning a failed run to the operator, the person operated on, the material or a third party. That is the condition the claim itself named. It was not met."@en ;
    pm:examinationState pm:casesWithDeviation ;
    pm:counterSearch pm:counterSearchFoundOpposition ;
    pm:counterSearchNote "Two searches, in two layers, over the compiled graph and then at the nodes returned. The first asked which transmissions in this holding name an observable sign of success or a stated term and then supply no excusing condition; it went first to the three addresses the claim names for itself and then over every tradition file by term. It found no case. The second asked which transmissions supply an excusing condition and put it outside the four places the claim enumerates; it found one, and the corpus it stands in is one of the nine witnesses. Not searched: anything outside this holding. The claim is about a form of wording and the holding now carries some ninety corpora, so the cheap search is the one that was run; a transmission outside it that refutes the claim would still refute it."@en ;
    pm:examinedBy "prima-materia, 2026-09-16" ;
    pm:protocolUpdated "2026-09-16" ;
    skos:note "The first address, and it is the strongest of the three because the sign is one a second person can observe. The eighth chapter of the Baopuzi lays a goose down on the nose and the mouth and makes the sign that it does not stir while the breath is let out (pmc:InaudibleAndUnevenBreath). Nothing in that chapter says what follows if the down stirs. What the same work supplies instead stands in its eighteenth chapter: to know the One is not hard, the hard thing is in the ending, and where a man forgets the guarding and is harmed by the hundred ghosts or pressed down in his sleep, he is to go into the courtyard, look at the assistant star and guard the One again, with a fallback for overcast weather (pmc:ShouyiZhongnan). The failure is in the operator's persistence and the remedy is more of the practice. The same chapter eight binds the circulation to the hours of living qi and says that in the hours of dead qi it is of no benefit, which assigns a further class of empty runs to the hour the operator chose."@en ;
    skos:note "The second address is the one where the sign and the excuse are printed in the same chapter, and it is the first witness of the claim. The fourth chapter of the Baopuzi gives the assay: joined with mercury and put to the fire, the elixir makes gold, and where the gold forms the drug is complete. Where it does not form, the drug is to be sealed and fired again for the same count of days, and then there is no case in which it does not form (pmc:JinchengYaocheng). The observable sign the claim sent the protocol to look for — the body turning gold in colour when the golden liquor enters the mouth (pmc:JinyeYijin) — stands four columns away from that clause and is covered by it."@en ;
    skos:note "The third address is the medical canon, and there the sign and the excuse are in adjacent chapters of one work. The fourteenth chapter names the case in which the body is worn out, the blood exhausted and the treatment establishes nothing, and gives it a name: the spirit does not lend itself (pmc:Shenbushi). The node entered from it already says that the passage supplies no mark by which the condition could have been established beforehand. That is the excuse for the ten-day term and for everything else in the corpus that could come out empty."@en ;
    skos:note "The deviation, and it stands inside a witness. The thirteenth chapter of the same medical canon asks why the ancients cured by shifting the essence and transforming the qi, so that the incantation after the cause sufficed, while now drugs are used within and needle and stone without, and some are cured and some are not. Its answer is not a defect of the operator, of the patient, of the material or of a third party. It is the age: in high antiquity men lived among the birds and beasts with no burden of longing within and no obligation of office without, the evil could not enter deeply, and the incantation was enough; the present age is not so, and therefore the incantation can no longer bring anything to an end (pmc:ZhuyouGujinYi). The empty run is assigned, and it is assigned to a fifth place the claim's enumeration does not carry."@en ;
    skos:note "What the deviation does and does not cost the claim. The first clause stands: the transmission does supply a condition, it does supply it in advance, and the condition is not an outcome a further run could establish — an age is even further out of reach of a further run than a defect of the operator, because no run can be moved into it. What fails is the enumeration in the middle, which was read off nine witnesses that all happened to name a party. The corrected wording would say that the condition is located anywhere other than in an outcome a further run could establish, and would name the four parties and the age as the values found so far. The statement is not rewritten here: a claim is corrected where it is examined, and what a later reader needs is the protocol beside it and not a tidied sentence."@en ;
    skos:note "Two near-misses, recorded because they bound the claim rather than break it. The Sami material reports two men who set a term, named the sign they demanded, received nothing and destroyed the idol and the drum without explaining the failure away (pmc:AbandonmentAfterFailure); the counter-search that preceded the claim had already found it, and it does not refute, because it reports conduct and not a rule, and because both cases stand in a missionary's chapter on conversion. The Oglala corpus names three things its means cannot reach at all — the Moon and the Wind cannot be influenced by ceremony, and the potency of the Sun can be imparted to nothing, so that a fetish of the Sun cannot be prepared (pmc:WhatCeremonyCannotReach). That is a limit set before the operation rather than an excuse supplied after it, and a transmission that forbids the attempt never has an empty run to place. It is the nearest thing in this holding to a corpus that lets an outcome count, and it works by not operating."@en ;
    skos:note "What the protocol is worth for the next examination. The claim survives with a wider consequent and is now harder to falsify than it was, which is a loss and should be said plainly: every widening of where the excuse may sit moves the claim further from anything that could come out against it. The place where it could still fail is the one the first search could not reach — a transmission outside this holding that names a term, lets it run out and then says of its own method that it does not work. The Pulling Book of the second century before this era, opened in the same run, was read with that question in hand and answered it the other way: knocking the teeth on waking prevents decay, and where there is decay already, the instruction is to knock them more (pmc:YinshuKouchi). That is the same two-clause shape as the assay of the fourth chapter, four hundred years earlier, and it is entered as the tenth witness rather than as a counter-case."@en ;
    skos:note "The procedural point, and it is the reason to run the second search separately in future. The first search asked which transmissions carry no excuse and it found nothing, which is what it would have found in the run that wrote the claim. The second asked which carry an excuse pointed the wrong way, and it returned a case in one query, from a corpus that had been a witness for weeks. The recommendation in prima-materia#726 was written before this protocol was run and this is its first test: the second counter-search is not a refinement of the first, it is a different question, and the material it reaches is not reachable from the terms of the first."@en .
